---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL } from '../data/site';

const email = LEGAL.contactEmail;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Acceptable Use Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  path="/acceptable-use/"
  lede="The rules for using DummyLead responsibly and lawfully, especially around recording calls and handling the people your seeds capture."
  description="DummyLead Acceptable Use Policy: prohibited uses, your call-recording and consent obligations, and how we enforce responsible use."
>
  <p>
    This Acceptable Use Policy ("AUP") is part of our
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> and governs how you may use DummyLead.
    Because DummyLead records calls and captures messages, using it responsibly
    is not optional. Violating this policy can result in suspension or
    termination without refund.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Your responsibility for recording and consent</h2>
  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      DummyLead gives you the technical ability to record calls and capture
      messages. It does <strong>not</strong> give you the legal right to do so.
      That right depends on the laws where you and the people contacting your
      seeds are located, and you are solely responsible for having it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>You agree that, for every seed you place, you will:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Determine which call-recording, wiretapping, eavesdropping, and consent
      laws apply, including laws that require the consent of
      <strong>all</strong> parties to a call;
    </li>
    <li>
      Obtain and maintain every consent, notice, and lawful basis those laws
      require before recording or capturing any interaction;
    </li>
    <li>
      Use captured data only for legitimate auditing, quality, training, and
      compliance purposes; and
    </li>
    <li>
      Keep your own records of the consents and lawful bases you rely on.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Prohibited uses</h2>
  <p>You may not use DummyLead to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Break any law or regulation, or infringe anyone's rights;</li>
    <li>
      Record, monitor, or intercept communications without the consent or lawful
      basis required by applicable law;
    </li>
    <li>
      Stalk, harass, threaten, defraud, dox, blackmail, or unlawfully surveil any
      person;
    </li>
    <li>
      Target or build profiles of individuals based on protected characteristics,
      or use captured data to discriminate unlawfully in employment or otherwise;
    </li>
    <li>
      Send spam or unlawful marketing, or place seeds in order to entrap or
      defame a person rather than to audit a lead process;
    </li>
    <li>
      Impersonate a real person without authorization, or use a real person's
      identity (rather than a fictitious persona) as a seed;
    </li>
    <li>
      Upload malware, attempt to breach security, probe or scan the service, or
      circumvent usage limits or billing;
    </li>
    <li>
      Resell, sublicense, or provide the service to third parties except as
      expressly permitted;
    </li>
    <li>
      Use captured recordings or data in a way that violates the privacy or
      employment rights of the people recorded.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Telephony and messaging conduct</h2>
  <p>
    Seed phone numbers and inboxes are for receiving and auditing contact, not
    for outbound campaigns. You may not use DummyLead numbers or inboxes to make
    bulk outbound calls or texts, to send unlawful or deceptive messages, or in
    any way that violates the rules of carriers, messaging providers, or
    anti-spam and telemarketing laws.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Fair use and system integrity</h2>
  <p>
    Don't do anything that degrades the service for others: no excessive
    automated load beyond documented limits, no attempts to reverse engineer or
    disrupt the platform, and no use that risks the security or availability of
    the service.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Reporting and enforcement</h2>
  <p>
    Report suspected violations to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We may
    investigate, and we may suspend or terminate accounts that violate this
    policy, with or without notice depending on severity. We may also remove
    content or report unlawful activity to authorities where required. Suspension
    or termination for a violation does not entitle you to a refund.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the service and the law evolve. Changes take
    effect on the updated effective date above, and continued use means you
    accept them.
  </p>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Not legal advice.</strong> Recording-consent law is genuinely
      complex and varies by country and US state. This policy shifts
      responsibility to the Customer, but it does not replace advice from a
      qualified attorney about how you and your customers may lawfully operate.
    </p>
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
